<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29836" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mŭlĭĕrārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		mulier, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a woman</i>
			(mostly postclass.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: manus, <i>the band sent by
				Clodia</i>, Cic Cael. 28, 66: voluptas, Auct. ap. Trebell.
			Trig. Tyrann. 6, 7.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mŭlĭĕrārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>a lover of
				women</i>, <i><span class="en">Cat. 25, 5</span></i> (dub.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">al munerarios),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Capitol. Albin. 11, 7</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Isid. 10, 107</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
